      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): reject IPv6 zone IDs in gateway endpoint URLs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGateway endpoint URLs with IPv6 interface zones — e.g. `ws://[fe80::1%25eth0]` — passed cleartext validation but stored a scoped host that OkHttp's URL-string WebSocket path cannot dial reliably, leading to confusing connect failures after UI validation succeeded.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n**Fail-closed:** reject scoped IPv6 hosts at parse time via `normalizeGatewayConnectionHost()` returning empty when `%` is present, instead of silently stripping the zone (which can target the wrong link-local interface).\n\nOkHttp `Request.Builder.url(String)` cannot represent scoped IPv6 authorities; explicit rejection gives operators a clear invalid-URL outcome rather than a silent endpoint change.\n\n## User Impact\n\nScoped IPv6 gateway URLs are rejected during endpoint parsing instead of appearing valid and then failing at connect time. Bare IPv6 literals (e.g. `::1`, `fe80::1` without zone) continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Unit tests**\n- `GatewayConfigResolverTest.parseGatewayEndpointRejectsLinkLocalIpv6ZoneCleartextWsUrls`\n- `GatewayConfigResolverTest.parseGatewayEndpointRejectsSecureIpv6ZoneUrls`\n\n**Local proof (Windows, branch `56f96f406b`)**\n```powershell\ncd apps/android\n.\\gradlew.bat :app:testPlayDebugUnitTest `\n  --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.GatewayConfigResolverTest.parseGatewayEndpointRejectsLinkLocalIpv6ZoneCleartextWsUrls `\n  --tests ai.openclaw.app.ui.GatewayConfigResolverTest.parseGatewayEndpointRejectsSecureIpv6ZoneUrls\n```\n- Result: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 53s`\n- JUnit: 2 tests, 0 failures\n\n**ClawSweeper follow-up:** replaced zone-stripping with explicit rejection per review feedback (avoid silent interface change).\n",
        "branch": "fix/android-gateway-ipv6-zone-host",
